5. The said principles and directions have been recently reaffirmed and reiterated by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Md. Asfak Alam vs. State of Jharkhand & Another, Criminal Appeal No. 2207 of 2023, decided on 31.07.2023, wherein the Court reiterated the binding nature of the guidelines laid down in Arnesh Kumar (supra), emphasising their continued applicability in similarly situated cases.
Hence, in light of the authoritative pronouncements of the Hon'ble Supreme Court in State of Haryana & Others vs.
Bhajan Lal & Others, 1992 Supp. (1) SCC 335; Neeharika Infrastructure Pvt. Ltd. vs. State of Maharashtra, AIR 2021 SC 1918; and Leelavati Devi @ Leelawati & Another vs. State of U.P., Special Leave to Appeal (Crl.) No. 3262/2021 decided on 07.10.2021, the prayer of the petitioner seeking quashing of the F.I.R. at the threshold stage cannot be acceded to.
However, such action must be taken strictly in adherence to the procedural safeguards and guidelines laid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Arnesh Kumar and Md. Asfak Alam (supra).
